HST Office: the default document colour theme is named "HST Office", not "LibreOffice".

Format ▸ Theme lists the bundled colour themes by name, and a saved .docx/.pptx/.xlsx carries the
theme's name, so "LibreOffice" was user-facing text. The theme file keeps its name; the code that looks
the default theme up by name follows the new name. The colour palette list already shows the
"libreoffice" palette as "HST Office" (hst-debrand.patch), and the selected palette is stored under
that display name, so existing profiles keep their palette.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: CppunitTest_sw_core_theme (a document whose theme is named "LibreOffice" keeps its name and colours;
new documents get "HST Office"); tests/runtime/check-no-libreoffice-ui.py.
